commit_sha":"46f2224338e42dd9bdf5b41b42fe9fd4a5c3adb2","position":"1785515615148319001-ec496689-42db-4f7b-9dd0-f37852d34447"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"06f1f14dd947ee64c23603076ac191bc69e6dc2a4c26d420cfc2b2bd1e3bdc42","event_uuid":"1af7d3d0-ebc9-4027-b3b0-fab1ab1e3a98","position":{"commit_sha":"1eacf120ea7ad424ebeb944a544b470ceaa67efb","position":"1785516214544661456-1af7d3d0-ebc9-4027-b3b0-fab1ab1e3a98"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"52d5d6e0-1933-4be1-9d52-bba891ba7553","comments":[],"created_at":1785339376904855001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cb3bd3c9-b1a6-47aa-a54f-63ebc04985cd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"544e-0a25-eabb-4220"},{"link_uuid":"c984bfcc-421e-4c4a-81a6-0b4d2c7cf308","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c36c-357a-2900-4ed7"},{"link_uuid":"0d956f77-73e7-4de0-a7d2-46ccf8ea6d13","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"acb2-1823-2f0d-415b"}],"description":"# AGENTS.md tells agents to override `default_assignee` with a bare handle, which reconcile then clears\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`AGENTS.md` — the canonical, launch-loaded agent guidance — instructs agents to claim with an\nexplicit assignee in **three** places:\n\n- `AGENTS.md:75` — \"`claim <id> --assignee <you>` … as the FIRST step of working a ticket\"\n- `AGENTS.md:106` — \"**Grab work atomically** — `claim <id> --assignee <you>`\"\n- `AGENTS.md:238` (library quick reference) — `rebar.claim(tid[\"id\"], assignee=\"me\")`\n\nTwo problems compound:\n\n1. **It instructs an override of a setting that exists precisely to get this right.**\n   `rebar.toml:66` configures `default_assignee = \"joeoakhart@navapbc.com\"`, and\n   `_commands/claim.py:124-125` applies it **only** when `--assignee` is omitted\n   (`if assignee is None`). Because `AGENTS.md` says to always pass `--assignee`, the\n   configured default is **never** reached on the agent path.\n2. **\"`<you>`\" / `assignee=\"me\"` invite a bare handle.** An agent substitutes its own\n   identity — e.g. `RebarBotNava`, or literally `me` as the library example shows — and\n   `AGENTS.md` gives no hint that the value must be Jira-resolvable.\n\nThe consequence is a silent revert. The reconciler cannot resolve a bare handle to a Jira\nuser, treats the ticket as unassigned, and the inbound differ writes `assignee=\"\"` back over\nthe local value. Work ends up attributed to nobody.\n\n`docs/config.md:397-400` already documents the requirement correctly — \"Use a **Jira-resolvable\nidentity** (email or accountId) … a bare, ambiguous handle (e.g. `joe`) is left unassigned\nrather than mis-assigned (bug 544e)\" — so the two documents **contradict each other**, and the\none agents actually read at launch is the wrong one. `AGENTS.md` never mentions\n`default_assignee` at all.\n\nThis is the documented failure mode of closed bug `544e-0a25-eabb-4220`, and story\n`c36c-357a-2900-4ed7` added `default_assignee` specifically to fix it — but `AGENTS.md` was\nnever updated to stop overriding it, so the fix does not reach agents.\n\n## Evidence (observed live, epic e369)\n\nClaimed the epic and story J1 with `--assignee RebarBotNava`, following `AGENTS.md`. Both\nreported success (`CLAIMED: acb2-… (assignee: RebarBotNava)`) and both later read back\n`assignee = ''`.\n\nThe event log proves the store write was correct and that no event ever wrote the empty string:\n\n```\nticket: CLAIM acb2-1823-2f0d-415b\n  EDIT.json -> \"data\":{\"fields\":{\"assignee\":\"RebarBotNava\"}}\n```\n\nEvery subsequent assignee-bearing EDIT also wrote `\"RebarBotNava\"`. The `''` therefore comes\nfrom a later reconciler-authored EDIT, exactly as session log `bb27-06bf-b868-42c7` recorded\nwith a live reproduction:\n\n> \"Event log for 3d3d: claim wrote EDIT {assignee:\\\"joe\\\"}; ~143s later a reconciler-authored\n> EDIT wrote {assignee:\\\"\\\"} — the clobber. Live API: validate_assignee_exists(\\\"joe\\\")\n> REJECTED (\\\"3 Joes, ambiguous\\\"); \\\"joeoakhart@navapbc.com\\\" RESOLVED to accountId\n> 712020:6471376f-…\"\n\nControl: throwaway probe tickets (not Jira-bound) **retained** `RebarBotNava` indefinitely,\nconfirming the clear is reconcile-side and not a `claim` parsing or persistence defect.\n\nNote `claimed_session` and `claim_harness` survive the clobber, so the claim is still\nattributable — but `assignee`, which `list`/`ready`/`next-batch` and every human reader use,\nis not.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the guidance, not the code — `claim`'s explicit-wins precedence is correct and\n`default_assignee` already works.\n\n1. **`AGENTS.md`** — change the claim instruction to omit `--assignee` so the configured\n   default applies: `claim <id>` (noting it auto-assigns `ticket.default_assignee`). Where an\n   explicit assignee is genuinely needed, state that it MUST be a Jira-resolvable identity\n   (email/accountId), never a bare handle, with a one-line pointer to\n   `docs/config.md#ticketdefault_assignee`. Update all three sites (`:75`, `:106`, `:238` —\n   the library example `assignee=\"me\"` is the worst offender).\n2. Consider a **warning at claim time** when an explicit assignee is a bare handle (no `@`,\n   not an accountId shape) while a `default_assignee` is configured — turning a silent\n   revert into a visible nudge. Optional; the doc fix is the blocking part.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `AGENTS.md`'s claim guidance no longer instructs an unconditional `--assignee` override; it\n      shows `claim <id>` and states that `ticket.default_assignee` is applied automatically\n- [ ] all three sites (`AGENTS.md:75`, `:106`, and the `:238` library example) are updated\n      consistently, and `assignee=\"me\"` no longer appears as a recommended value\n- [ ] where an explicit assignee is documented, `AGENTS.md` states it must be Jira-resolvable\n      (email/accountId) and links to `docs/config.md#ticketdefault_assignee`\n- [ ] `AGENTS.md` and `docs/config.md` no longer contradict each other on assignee identity\n- [ ] a fresh agent following ONLY `AGENTS.md` produces a ticket whose assignee survives a\n      reconcile pass (verifiable by claiming a scratch ticket and confirming the assignee is\n      non-empty after one bridge cycle)","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"the claim guidance at :75, :106 and the library example at :238 that instruct the override"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"already-correct guidance AGENTS.md must stop contradicting"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","544e-0a25-eabb-4220"],["relates_to","c36c-357a-2900-4ed7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f8a8d4ff-b4d4-4bfb-a1b6-4db59fa944e6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5cc0-1005-018e-4085","ticket_type":"bug","title":"AGENTS.md tells agents to override default_assignee with a bare handle, which reconcile clears","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d9336ecb-9ea1-42f3-a58c-0e43677e01c6","cb3bd3c9-b1a6-47aa-a54f-63ebc04985cd","c984bfcc-421e-4c4a-81a6-0b4d2c7cf308","0d956f77-73e7-4de0-a7d2-46ccf8ea6d13","8fa5e50f-bf71-46f5-8b9b-b4a40c1efa4e","f8a8d4ff-b4d4-4bfb-a1b6-4db59fa944e6","ec496689-42db-4f7b-9dd0-f37852d34447","1af7d3d0-ebc9-4027-b3b0-fab1ab1e3a98"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785516214544661457,"uuid":"dd04e616-ed56-45c8-879e-4a335f519a3a"}